From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:25:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] queue an <img> under its latest request only

load_image added the node to the new URL's pending list but never
took it off the previous one. Both responses then targeted it, and the
first to land won: a stale success painted the old image over the new
src, and a stale 404 reported the node broken. The page-script shim
keeps the first terminal state per node, so that 404 also swallowed the
real load event (WPT img.complete.html "async src complete test").

Drop the node's Image entries from every pending list before queueing
the new request. The old fetch stays in flight and still fills the
image cache.
---
 src/mutator.rs | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mutator.rs b/src/mutator.rs
index 73a22dc..1618a59 100644
--- a/src/mutator.rs
+++ b/src/mutator.rs
@@ -1650,6 +1650,16 @@ impl<'doc> DocumentMutator<'doc> {
     }

     fn load_image(&mut self, target_id: NodeId) {
+        // An <img> waits on its latest request only. Changing
+        // src left the node queued under the previous URL too, so
+        // whichever response landed first won: a stale success painted
+        // the old image, and a stale 404 reported the node broken (the
+        // shim keeps the first terminal state), swallowing the real
+        // load event (WPT img.complete.html "async src complete test").
+        // The old fetch stays in flight and still fills the cache.
+        for waiting in self.doc.pending_images.values_mut() {
+            waiting.retain(|(id, ty)| !(*id == target_id && matches!(ty, ImageType::Image)));
+        }
         if let Some(raw_src) = self.select_image_url(target_id) {
             if !raw_src.is_empty() {
                 // Fallible resolve. `img.src = "http://"`
